  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nThe upper trough will steer out of the region Sunday, keeping \nthe area under northwest flow and seasonal normal temperatures.\nMonday through the end of the extended period, a ridge of high \npressure will build back over the northwest region, leading to a\nreturn of dry conditions and a steady warming trend through \nmidweek. Tuesday and Wednesday are still expecting to see \ntemperatures 10 to 20 degrees above normal. Come Thursday, a dry\nshortwave trough from the Pacific coast will dig across our area.\nThere is considerable guidance uncertainty about this trough, \nbut for now, a potential cooling trend with dry conditions will\nremain for Thursday.",
